<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12551" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδρύπτω</span></b> , aor. 1
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέδρυψα</span>: aor. 2
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέδρῠφον</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tear off the skin, lacerate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή μιν ἀποδρύφοι ἑλκυστάζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.187
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή σε νέοι διὰ δώματ᾽ ἐρύσσωσ᾽ . .
					ἀποδρύψωσί τε πάντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.480
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρκας ὀνύχεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.267
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ χειρῶν ῥινοὶ ἀπέδρυφθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.435
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				426
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδρυφθῆναι χαλάζη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.365
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>):—
				Med.
			, <i>scrape oneself, grow thin,</i> dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.51
			</span></i>.</div>
